{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"INVESTIGATION (per operator hold): ADR-0035 + fsck_repair.py + rebuild path, vs the\nxenops plan. Findings:\n\n(a) IS THE LIVE INCIDENT COVERED BY THE EXISTING DOOR? YES. The observed orphan is a\nCOMMENT — in _AUTO_RECOVER_ORPHAN_TYPES (fsck_repair.py:38). Both fsck doors reach a\nfull-log rebuild that captures it: (1) fsck --repair-snapshots -> repair_or_plan ->\nrebuild_with_restore -> rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log (reduce include_retired=True,\nsnapshots stripped, no positional short-circuit; crash-safe .snapshot-rebuild.bak\nsentinel; b636 fail-closed guard when a prior snapshot cites sources absent from\ndisk); (2) fsck --repair (A3 cluster) -> _repair_ticket, which routes BY TYPE:\nauto-recover -> rebuild, order-sensitive -> human triage, never auto-written. The\nnew snapshot cites the orphan; fsck goes clean. The refuted premise is confirmed\nrefuted: \"no repair door\" was wrong.\n\n(b) ACTUAL GAPS FOUND:\n\nG1 (SERIOUS, and the real bug worth a ticket): the NATURAL RE-FOLD DESTROYS\nORPHANS. On origin/main, a compaction whose candidate set contains [orphan,\nsnapshot] (sweep via --skip-sync, compact-on-close, or once foldable live events\ncross the threshold) reduces via whole-dir replay -> positional skip buries the\norphan's EFFECT, yet source_uuids includes the orphan's uuid and the file is\nretired. Result: the effect is permanently lost AND the ORPHAN_EVENT signal is\nerased (uuid now cited -> fsck clean). The window between orphan creation and the\nnext natural fold is the ONLY time the existing door can fire. Verified by my RED\ntest run: refold rc=0, comment still invisible, file retired, uuid cited. ADR-0035\nOption 3 prevents new orphans at fold time but does not protect an\nalready-landed orphan from the NEXT fold.\n\nG2: doctor --repair does not route ORPHAN_EVENT anywhere (merged 1771 state: links\n+ dirty + locks only). The heal is reachable only via the separate fsck flags.\nCosmetic-to-moderate: two operator doors, one blind to this class.\n\nG3: nothing AUTO-triggers detection or heal on the writer path after a union\nmerge. sync only HINTS at fsck on conflict; ensure_fresh and the compact trigger do\nno orphan scanning. Detection waits for a human/external watchdog to run fsck.\nNote G1 makes this worse: waiting silently converts repairable damage into\nunrepairable loss.\n\nG4 (policy drift between the two existing fsck doors): --repair-snapshots'\nrepair_or_plan triggers on ANY ORPHAN_EVENT finding and rebuilds whole-ticket\nWITHOUT the type routing; --repair enforces auto-recover vs human-triage. The\nrouting discipline exists on one door only (possibly intentional as an explicit\nopt-in, but worth confirming).\n\n(c) ORDERING: YES, MOOT — full-log rebuild replays the complete raw log in HLC\nfilename total order, so an absorbed orphan takes effect AT ITS TIMESTAMP position;\ndeterministic and equal to what a clone that had always seen the event computes.\nThat is the canonical semantics. My change 1779's pinned \"snapshot state, then\norphans by ts\" ordering CONTRADICTS it (e.g. orphan ts between c0 and c1: rebuild\nyields [c0, middle, c1, c2]; 1779 yields [c0, c1, middle, ...]) — two repair doors\nwould produce different states from identical bytes. 1779 also absorbs ALL types\nblindly, bypassing the triage routing — the exact hazard the routing guards.\n\nDISPOSITION OF CHANGE 1779: marked WIP (done, REST 200). Its doctor/--absorb-orphans\ndoor duplicates the existing repair and must not land as-is. Two pieces remain\ngenuinely useful if the ticket is rewritten to G1: (i) the defer guard\n(pre-snapshot candidates never fold without their governing snapshot — closes a\nsilent-burial hazard adjacent to G1); (ii) making the fold orphan-AWARE — but the\ncorrect shape is likely: fold EXCLUDES un-cited pre-snapshot events from\nfold_files/source_uuids (leaving them live so the fsck signal and repair window\nsurvive), rather than absorbing with novel ordering. Absorption, if wanted at fold\ntime, should reuse full-log-total-order semantics and respect the type routing.\n\nRecommend: rewrite the ticket to G1 (fold must not destroy orphan evidence), with\nG2/G3/G4 as separate follow-up candidates. I will rework or abandon 1779 to match."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786724510726142001,"uuid":"0609d7a8-da96-46e7-a44f-21939b3a16a3"}